{"page":21918,"revision":1327936046,"ref":"o1","kind":"subject","cue":"lead","strength":"normal","name":"Normal subgroup","span":[0,754],"text":"In abstract algebra, a normal subgroup (also known as an invariant subgroup or self-conjugate subgroup) is a subgroup that is invariant under conjugation by members of the group of which it is a part. In other words, a subgroup $N$ of the group $G$ is normal in $G$ if and only if $gng^{-1} \\in N$ for all $g \\in G$ and $n \\in N.$ The usual notation for this relation is $N \\triangleleft G.$","math":[{"form":"math","tex":"N","source":"<math>N</math>","span":[514,528]},{"form":"math","tex":"G","source":"<math>G</math>","span":[542,556]},{"form":"math","tex":"G","source":"<math>G</math>","span":[570,584]},{"form":"math","tex":"gng^{-1} \\in N","source":"<math>gng^{-1} \\in N</math>","span":[600,627]},{"form":"math","tex":"g \\in G","source":"<math>g \\in G</math>","span":[636,656]},{"form":"math","tex":"n \\in N.","source":"<math>n \\in N.</math>","span":[661,682]},{"form":"math","tex":"N \\triangleleft G.","source":"<math>N \\triangleleft G.</math>","span":[723,754]}],"links":[{"title":"Abstract algebra"},{"title":"Subgroup"},{"title":"Invariant (mathematics)"},{"title":"Inner automorphism"},{"title":"Group (mathematics)"}],"citations":["o2"],"hash":"sha256:f95c903b27631540a8f7b71832460fae4a91c0758f13143d3d531d2e5c92c01e","extractor":"m2/v0.3.8"}
